::ENG4_U06_L06_GP_Q01::[MLA.ENG4.C.03] Multimedia scenario: A senior project team will publish a multimedia text about youth financial literacy using a written introduction, infographic, narration, source credits, and a shareable digital format. Which option best supports publication-ready multimedia communication? {
=A. Match each media element to a clear purpose and make sure all sources are credited.#Correct. This answer best applies the lesson skill with clear reasoning, evidence, and audience awareness.
~B. Add more media elements even if they repeat the same idea.#Incorrect. Review the lesson and choose the option that best supports purpose, clarity, credibility, access, and publication readiness.
~C. Publish quickly because multimedia products do not need revision.#Incorrect. Review the lesson and choose the option that best supports purpose, clarity, credibility, access, and publication readiness.
~D. Use borrowed visuals without credit if they make the product more attractive.#Incorrect. Review the lesson and choose the option that best supports purpose, clarity, credibility, access, and publication readiness.
}

